# Exhaustiveness checking for bare NominalVariant scrutinee via ConstructorSignature::from_nominal_variant.
# A single-constructor type declaration produces a bare NominalVariant (not wrapped in Union).
# When the match does not cover the constructor, a non-exhaustive error must be raised.
# This exercises the from_nominal_variant path (not from_union).
[
  MyTag: [type [MyTag value: Int]]

  bad-match: [fn [let s@MyTag]
    [match s
      Int: 0
    ]
  ]

  result: 42
]
=== out
non-exhaustive match: missing coverage for [MyTag _]
